        "original_id": "1399617f-89fe-52e1-8761-d61718b2d4b6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tie Domi, Bill Watters, Paul Beeston, Bobby Orr\n- Organizations: Maple Leaf Sports & Entertainment, Toronto Maple Leafs, Toronto Blue Jays\n- Teams: Ontario Raiders, Toronto Rock\n- Places: Toronto, Maple Leaf Gardens\n\nFacts:\n- Tahir \"Tie\" Domi was born on November 1, 1969, and he is a retired Canadian professional ice hockey player of Albanian origin.\n- Maple Leaf Sports & Entertainment considered purchasing the Ontario Raiders but did not complete the purchase.\n- A group including Bill Watters, the then Assistant General Manager of the Toronto Maple Leafs, Paul Beeston, the former president of the Toronto Blue Jays, Tie Domi of the Toronto Maple Leafs, and former NHL player Bobby Orr bought the Ontario Raiders for $250,000.\n- After buying the Ontario Raiders, the group promptly relocated the team to Toronto's Maple Leaf Gardens and rebranded it as the Toronto Rock.",
